            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for a husband, then the Arabic for a wife."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: طفل",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "طفل — ṭifl — \"a child\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "طفل (ṭifl) is built on the native Arabic root ṭ-f-l, \"a child, an infant\" (Lane). Ṭifl is Lane's word for a young child."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
